cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pythonic_biotools: Standalone Python Implementations of Bioinformatics, Oncology, Clinical Trial, and Statistical Genetics Libraries"
message: >-
  If you use pythonic_biotools in your research, please cite both this software
  repository and the original peer-reviewed methodology publications for every
  specific algorithm or statistical model used in your analysis (citations are
  provided in the root README.md and in each package's README.md).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tanaka
    given-names: Yutaro
repository-code: "https://github.com/gillanilab/pythonic_biotools"
url: "https://gillanilab.github.io/pythonic_biotools/"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  pythonic_biotools provides 70 standalone, PEP 561-typed Python implementations
  of published R, Bioconductor, CRAN, C++, and Fortran methods across cancer
  somatic genomics, ctDNA liquid biopsy, mutational signatures, Mendelian
  randomization, colocalization, causal TWAS, multivariate statistical genetics,
  bulk and spatial transcriptomics deconvolution, single-cell mixed models,
  quantitative proteomics, epigenomics, and clinical trial survival biostatistics.
  Every package supports both numerically hardened Pythonic defaults
  (settings="default") and strict upstream replication (settings="R_default")
  without requiring rpy2 or external R sessions. Please always cite the original
  methodology papers alongside this software collection.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - computational-biology
  - cancer-genomics
  - liquid-biopsy
  - statistical-genetics
  - mendelian-randomization
  - colocalization
  - spatial-transcriptomics
  - single-cell-omics
  - proteomics
  - epigenomics
  - survival-analysis
  - clinical-trials
  - python
